<title>USA: Novartis disagrees with FDA finding.</title>
<headline>Novartis disagrees with FDA finding.</headline>
<dateline>SUMMIT, N.J. 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Novartis Consumer Health, a unit of Swiss-based Novartis AG and the makers of Ex-Lax, said it strongly disagrees with a Food and Drug Administration panel's concerns about phenolphthalein, an ingredient in laxatives.</p>
<p>The FDA's Carcinogenicity Assessment Committee found that phenolphthalein may cause cancer in mice when given in high doses.</p>
<p>Novartis said it questioned the validity of the study and intends to advocate for the continued availability of phenolphthalein.</p>
<p>No serious adverse conditions have been reported in connection with phenolphthalein for nearly 100 years, Novartis said.</p>
</text>
